{"format":"gravitas.sun-frames","formatVersion":1,"prompt":194,"part":2,"title":"The Sun, 4 to 17 May 2024: HMI continuum pictures, the geometry of each and a daily irradiance series","displayOnly":"Each picture is an SDO HMI continuum BROWSE picture, a 1,024 pixel display picture; its source says browse products are not intended for science analysis. Heliographic positions read from it are an instructional measurement, labelled not astrometry (delegated ruling D-R10-92): they carry the placement uncertainty and the foreshortening and say nothing about the picture’s photometry or its own world coordinates, which it does not have.","northUp":"The pictures have solar north up and east left: pImageDeg is 0 for the pixel to heliographic conversion. pSkyDeg is Horizons’ NP.ang (the pole against celestial north) and is not used for it.","sources":{"frames":{"what":"SDO HMI continuum, quick-look browse picture, 1,024 pixels, one a day at 12:00 UT","url":"https://sdo.gsfc.nasa.gov/assets/img/browse/2024/05/DD/2024MMDD_120000_1024_HMIIC.jpg","credit":"SDO/NASA and the HMI science team","retrieved":"2026-10-27","sha256Of":"each file in days[].sha256"},"ephemeris":{"what":"JPL Horizons API 1.2: target 10 (Sun), observer 500@399 (geocentre), daily 12:00 UT; quantities 14 (ObsSub-LON, ObsSub-LAT), 17 (NP.ang), 20 (delta, deldot); the Sun’s rotation model is Horizons’ IAU_SUN","credit":"NASA/JPL Solar System Dynamics, Horizons","retrieved":"2026-10-27","sha256":"421056e88ccb67de1546f9115d78b406b55c86de018b6212e2f596e10d8f44f7"},"irradiance":{"what":"LASP LISIRD tsis_tsi_24hr: TSIS-1 TIM total solar irradiance, daily, at 1 AU and at the Earth, with its measurement uncertainty","instrument":"TSIS-1 TIM (Total Irradiance Monitor)","credit":"LASP/TSIS-1 TIM team (the citation requested by the data provider)","retrieved":"2026-10-27","sha256":"423362b09328a3ea6781061bfb9d2d0904b2a2923c64c6d7876d976aa62acb3c","note":"The file has 13 rows, JD 2460435 to 2460447. The first six (2024-05-04 to 2024-05-09) are measured; the last seven are 0.0 with an uncertainty of 0.0, which are fill values, not a measurement of zero, and are marked fill here. 2024-05-17 is not in the file. This pack carries no irradiance value for 2024-05-10 to 2024-05-17."},"regionCounts":"NOAA SWPC solar region summaries were NOT retrieved. groupsRead is what the detector of this tool reads from the picture (dark clusters of at least 12 pixels, single linkage at 14 pixels), not NOAA’s numbered regions, and a split group counts as two."},"rules":{"imageNorth":"SDO browse frames have solar north up (helioprojective north is the image's up). The kernel's disk.pDeg is the position angle of the pole in the IMAGE, so it is 0 for these frames; Horizons' NP.ang (the pole's position angle against celestial north, about -23 degrees in May 2024) is carried in the sidecar for information and is NOT used for pixel to heliographic conversion. Leg e0.orientation holds this.","limbFit":"The disc centre and radius of each frame are measured, not assumed: luminance 0.299 R + 0.587 G + 0.114 B of the decoded pixels; 360 rays one degree apart from a coarse centre (the mean of the pixels above luminance 60) outward; the limb on a ray is where the luminance falls through half of the mean of the same ray's levels from 14 to 6 pixels inside the coarse radius, linearly interpolated; an algebraic circle fit with six passes that drop rays more than 1.0 pixel off the circle. Pixel coordinates have the centre of the first pixel at (0, 0).","spotDetector":"dark pixel: luminance below 0.62 times the 41 by 41 box mean of the luminance (the window clipped at the edges), more than 0 and inside 0.985 of the fitted radius. A cluster: single linkage of dark pixels at a Euclidean distance of 14 pixels or less. A group counted in a frame: a cluster of at least 12 dark pixels. A cluster's position: the mean of its dark pixels. This reads dark clusters, not NOAA region numbers, and a split group counts as two.","tracking":"A group's seed is a position on 2024-05-04: G1 (452, 422), G2 (593, 276), G3 (259, 654), each taken to the nearest cluster of at least 6 dark pixels within 40 pixels. The following day's expected position is the same heliographic latitude and Carrington longitude, converted with that day's centre, radius, B0 and L0 (solid co-rotation: the law's rates are not used); the group in that frame is the nearest cluster of at least 6 dark pixels within 40 pixels of it; a track ends when there is none or when the group's mu is below 0.25. The group's mark on a day is that cluster's position, with a placement sigma of 1.5 pixels (a cluster centroid is not a point).","usableDays":"a rate uses the days on which the group's mu is at least 0.35 (the kernel's own `precise` line); the days between mu 0.25 and 0.35 are kept in the sidecar for the foreshortening lesson and are used only in leg e1.limb","reference":"the primary law, Howard, Harvey and Forgach (1990), as in thresholds.json, and the 0.3 degree a day group scatter floor of thresholds.json"},"groups":{"G1":"the isolated small spot near the equator","G2":"the northern spread-out complex","G3":"the large southern group that grows during the window"},"marks":{"G1":{"sigmaPx":1.5,"marks":[{"day":0,"x":452.5,"y":421.9,"pixels":33},{"day":1,"x":563.6,"y":419.9,"pixels":27},{"day":2,"x":667.9,"y":423.6,"pixels":30},{"day":3,"x":763,"y":428.2,"pixels":32},{"day":4,"x":845.6,"y":433.8,"pixels":19},{"day":5,"x":911.8,"y":438.2,"pixels":13},{"day":6,"x":956.8,"y":443.8,"pixels":6}]},"G2":{"sigmaPx":1.5,"marks":[{"day":0,"x":602,"y":279.3,"pixels":164},{"day":1,"x":683.9,"y":283.1,"pixels":145},{"day":2,"x":751.6,"y":284.9,"pixels":81},{"day":3,"x":818.5,"y":286.7,"pixels":50},{"day":4,"x":872.9,"y":290.9,"pixels":30},{"day":5,"x":912.9,"y":298.2,"pixels":17}]},"G3":{"sigmaPx":1.5,"marks":[{"day":0,"x":257.8,"y":653.3,"pixels":78},{"day":1,"x":345.3,"y":651.2,"pixels":122},{"day":2,"x":438,"y":647.2,"pixels":130},{"day":3,"x":537,"